u_{	au}$, $	au^{-} ightarrow \pi^{-}\pi^{0}
u_{	au}$, and $	au^{-} ightarrow \pi^{-}\pi^{+}\pi^{-}
u_{	au}$. The spin orientation of the $	au$ leptons in these decays is reconstructed using the polarimeter-vector method. Assuming a dataset of $200$ million $	au^{+}	au^{-}$ events and accounting for experimental resolutions, we expect the observation of quantum entanglement and Bell inequality violation by the Belle-II experiment will be possible with a significance well in excess of five standard deviations.

